  "id": "COMPOUND:9138 - PROTEIN:1381",
  "verbalization": "Calcium gluconate is implicated in the regulation of Beclin-1 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that calcium gluconate targets 72 kDa type IV collagenase, which in turn is a target of two different compounds—N-[(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-7-methyloctanamide and Spongia-13(16),14-Dien-19-Oic Acid—both of which ultimately interact with Beclin-1. This indicates that calcium gluconate may modulate Beclin-1 through the activation or inhibition of downstream targets that are involved in autophagy-related processes. Additionally, calcium gluconate is also shown to target ATP synthase subunit a, which is a target of Puqiedine, and Puqiedine itself has a known interaction with Beclin-1. While the direct mechanism linking calcium gluconate to Beclin-1 remains unclear, the evidence suggests a potential role in autophagy regulation through the modulation of collagenase and ATP synthase subunit targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with calcium gluconate potentially influencing Beclin-1 through a network of molecular interactions that are still under investigation.",
